    "turn_text": "on YouTube or Rumble or whatever, or Twitch, after the show, not during the show, but the ones they do after the show, I'll take some questions, we'll do some Q&A. I'll end up doing some singing on there at the end of it as well. But the questions always are, how good do you feel about Tuesday? Where the questions are, how much weight do you give to the polls? The questions are, do you think they'll cheat? And my answer is always this. How do I think we're going to do it on Tuesday? I don't know. Go and vote. How much weight do you put into the polls? None. Act like your candidate's losing by 10. And do you think they'll cheat? I think they'd like to. I think that we're in a better position this time than we were four years ago. And by better position, I mean, we're going to have more observers going to be more volunteers on the ground. It's going to be harder for any hijinks to go on at the polling places. I also like that you've got people that aren't going to take it for granted that voting on election day is going to be easy or you can get it done. So I like that so many conservatives, which is abnormal, have gone and early voted. I also like who all have cell phones. You can be, as Chip Roy talked about earlier, or it might be Tony Gonzalez coming up, I think it's Chip Roy. You can be a citizen journalist. You can have your cell phone, and there's something going on. You just start rolling. You have actual video. Because people, they'll also come in there and they'll say things like, What do you think about blah, blah, blah story? I'm like, I've never heard of it. I've no idea what the blah, blah, blah story is. Send me a link. Send me your video. Send me the proof that you have. Now, there is a video that's out there and I have not been able to verify it, but it's in Kentucky and it shows somebody allegedly trying to vote. And they keep on trying to press Donald Trump and JD Vance and it won't take. But it will take if you do Kamala Harris and Tim Walz. I don't know if that's a real video or not. It doesn't look like it's been altered. And they actually back back out and show that it's the actual voting machine. Hopefully that problem has been solved if that was a problem. But again, let me say it again. This is still several days before the election. And we now have that video and we have the video in Pennsylvania. You've got, you know, people telling those waiting in line that the voting the line is going to stop here. Now, I'll give you in that district where they are to probably throughout the entire state, you're allowed if you're in line by 5 o'clock p.m. You're allowed to vote. That means if you're in line at 5 o'clock p.m. and it takes three more hours to get to the actual machine or to the actual polling place, too bad. You still get to go and vote. But they started putting up signs saying the line stops here at like 145. You can't do that. That's against the rules. So somebody took out their cell phone and started rolling. And now the questions have been put to the actual secretary of state, the county commissioners, because there's one woman there has some badge on, some langer around her neck saying, oh, you got to talk to the county commissioners. No, no, I don't. I know what the voting rules are. I'm in line at 145. You can't stop the line because you feel like it. So do I think they'll cheat? I think people would like to give themselves the best advantage they can. And that advantage needs to be stopped by you and me with our cell phones. Document it, document it and document it some more, okay? Because at the end of the day, we want a fair and free result. We want all of our franchises to be taken care of on Tuesday. I hope we get a result on Tuesday. I think one of two things is gonna happen. It's going to be a blowout and we get the result on Tuesday or it's going to be tight and we won't have the result for several days. Because the swing states all have different rules of how they do it. You have like Arizona made some announcement that it's going to take several days to find out who won. Why? Because Florida can do it that night. We'll know who wins Florida that night. Why can't Arizona do that? Or remember in 2020 Pennsylvania Trump was ahead by hundreds of thousands of votes woke up the next morning and he wasn't anymore. or Michigan, suddenly he was winning, then he was losing. Why can't they just know that night? I thought that the convenience of the machines was that you didn't have to count them by hand. The machine is that much faster than a human being could go. So why is it that in the places where they're not doing hand count ballots, you have machines that should be telling you very quickly, why are those the places where you have to wait several days? I also like that you've got to receive the ballot by the election day. I think it was Pennsylvania in 2020 that was saying as long as this postmarked by election day, we'll accept it up to eight days later or some crap like that. How stupid is that? That doesn't make any sense. So again, if it's a blowout, we're going to know that night. If it's tight, it's going to take a long time and probably a lot of court cases. And that could mean we won't even know who controls the House and the Senate until sometime into January. You never know. So that's why I see happening. So the answers are simple. How do you feel about Tuesday? I don't feel good. Go and vote. Act like you're 10 points down. How much weight do you put in the bowl? Zero. Well, they cheat. I think they'll try. But hopefully we're in place right now to worry we can stop that from happening. Kamala Harris is out there in the campaign trail again, but I want to start with Joe Biden. Joe Biden is cognitively gone. Every time he goes near a microphone now, he says something stupid or incoherent. Here's the latest. Remember the last guy when he was president said we're gonna have we have retired we have and say every week we're gonna have infrastructure week. What? Say what did he say? Something about infrastructure week. He said we're not the last guy we had to do that. We have got to have a retire infrastructure week. I'm pretty sure that's what he said. No? Yes, I think so. Okay. I could be off. Maybe I misunderstood. Maybe I misheard here again the leader of the free world. He has the nuclear codes. He's the president of",
