    "turn_text": "They didn't even come out of the Senate. They didn't make it to the House. That was garbage. It was 5,000 people a day could come in for seven days, 35,000 illegal entrants. And then all of a sudden you shut it down. But even though how long you shut it down, then you reopen it again. Then you get 5,000 a day for seven days again. And it would add two million more illegal aliens across the border every year. So in a perfect world, Trump wins. You've got the House in the Senate. How do you codify what he did in the first term and make it stick? Well, I think it starts with just is bringing transparency back to government. I mean, that's what I think so many people are frustrated. Just tell me the truth. And sometimes the truth isn't perfect. It shouldn't be perfect. But just as an American citizen, as a Texan, we deserve to know the truth. And so this is why I'll give you an example. You know, in March, I sat down with the director vice and I asked him two questions. I said, Hey, Patrick, how many convicted illegal aliens are in our country illegally? He said over He goes, Tony, it's a lot.",
